1
00:00:00,641 --> 00:00:01,891
(Past Leonard:)Yeah, experimental physics.

2
00:00:03,102 --> 00:00:04,392
(Past Sheldon:)Hmm.

3
00:00:05,771 --> 00:00:07,651
(Past Leonard:)-What is that?
-Doesn't concern you.

4
00:00:08,232 --> 00:00:10,572
(Past Sheldon:)You'll be going to the university
every day?

5
00:00:10,735 --> 00:00:12,025
(Leonard(voice off):)-Yes.
-Do you have a vehicle?

6
00:00:12,194 --> 00:00:14,074
(Past Leonard:)-A car.
-And you'd be willing to drive me?

7
00:00:14,238 --> 00:00:18,158
(Past Leonard:)-Well, can't you drive?
-I can.

8
00:00:19,577 --> 00:00:21,617
(Past Sheldon:)I choose not to.

9
00:00:22,330 --> 00:00:24,410
(Past Leonard:)Okay, I suppose I could drive you.

10
00:00:25,708 --> 00:00:29,588
-Well, what's a point in my favor, right?
-Why don't you let me do this?

11
00:00:30,379 --> 00:00:31,919
(Past Leonard:)Come on, I just asked.

12
00:00:36,427 --> 00:00:38,927
(Past Sheldon:)Last question.
In a post-apocalyptic world...

13
00:00:39,096 --> 00:00:41,596
(Past Sheldon:)...which task would you assign
the highest priority?

14
00:00:41,766 --> 00:00:45,436
(Past Sheldon:)Locating a sustainable food source,
reestablishing a functioning government...

15
00:00:45,603 --> 00:00:48,603
...procreation
or preserving the knowledge of mankind?

16
00:00:49,565 --> 00:00:51,945
(Past Leonard:)Uh, I'm gonna go with
preserving the knowledge.

17
00:00:52,109 --> 00:00:54,029
(Past Sheldon:)That's correct.

18
00:00:54,612 --> 00:01:00,022
FYI, I would've accepted
any answer other than procreating.

